  A "User Product" is either (1) a consumer product, or (2) anything
that is most likely to be found in a business or institutional
setting.  If conveying a covered work to a User Product, the
circumstances in which the work will be used must be such that it is
not normally used in a way that is not private.

  If you convey a covered work not as a User Product, you and the
party to which you convey it must have agreed to convey the
Corresponding Source along with the work for one year, with the
Corresponding Source made available to any licensee of the work.

