  10. Automatic Licensing of Downstream Recipients.

  Each time you convey a covered work, the recipient automatically
receives a license from the original licensors, to run, modify and
propagate that work, subject to this License.  You are not
responsible for enforcing third party compliance with this License.

  An "entity transaction" is a transfer of control of an organization,
or substantially all assets of one, or a merger or reorganization
of an organization.  If propagation of a covered work occurs in an
entity transaction, each party to the transaction that receives a
copy of the work also receives a license to run, modify and
propagate the work, subject to this License, along with every other
material embodiment of the work.

  11. Patents.

  A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes use under this
License of either the Program or a work based on the Program.  The
work to which the contributor has authorized such use is called the
contributor's "contributor version".

  A contributor's "essential patent claims" are all patent claims
controlled or owned by the contributor that would be infringed by
some manner, permitted by this License, of making, using, or selling
its contributor version, but would not be infringed if the contributor
version were not made, used, or sold.  For the purposes of this
section, "control" includes the right to grant patent licenses in a
manner consistent with the terms of this License.

  Each contributor grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
patent license under the contributor's essential patent claims, to
make, use, sell, offer for sale, import and otherwise run, modify and
propagate the contents of its contributor version.

  In the following three sections, a "patent license" is any express
agreement or commitment, however denominated, not to enforce a patent
(such as an express permission to practice a patent) but to license
patent rights in a manner that is consistent with the terms of this
License.

  If you convey a covered work, knowingly relying on a patent license,
and the Corresponding Source of the work is not available for anyone
to copy, distribute, modify, or make available on the public network
by means that are not reasonably available or by payment of a fee,
then you must either (1) cause the Corresponding Source to be so
available, or (2) arrange to deprive yourself of the benefit of the
patent license for this particular work, or (3) arrange, in a manner
consistent with the terms of this License, to extend the patent
license to downstream recipients.  "Knowingly relying" means you have
actual knowledge that, but for the patent license, your conveying the
covered work in a country, or your recipient's use of the covered work
in that country, would infringe one or more identifiable patents in
that country that you have reason to believe are valid.

  If, pursuant to or in connection with a single transaction or
arrangement, you convey a covered work, and the patent license is
granted to a particular recipient, covering the same work, the
patent license shall be automatically extended to all downstream
recipients of the covered work.

  A patent license is "discriminatory" if it does not include within
the scope of its coverage, the prohibition of exercising rights
granted under this License, or imposes conditions that prohibit
exercising those rights.  You may not convey a covered work if you
have arranged to depend on a patent license that is discriminatory.

  Nothing in this License shall be construed as excluding or limiting
any implied license or other defenses to infringement that may
otherwise apply under applicable law.

